  "id": "Wandsworth-2026_0841",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Erection of part single part two storey rear extension, rear mansard roof extension to main roof and above two storey outrigger, conversion of property into 5 self-contained flats (1 x 3-bed, 1 x 2-bed, 2 x 1-bed/2-person, 1 x 1-bed/1-person) with associated refuse and cycle storage, outside amenity space, hard and soft landscaping and boundary treatment.",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed extensions, by reason of their cumulative bulk, scale and proximity to neighbouring boundaries, would result in an overbearing and unneighbourly form of development that would materially harm the residential amenity of adjoining occupiers, particularly No.124 Church Lane. The proposed development is therefore contrary to policy LP2 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Housing SPD (2016).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed extensions, by reason of their design, scale and location, would fail to be subservient to the original host dwelling and its setting, would create excessive massing that dominates the host property and results in harm to the character and appearance of the surrounding townscape and setting of the adjacent Totterdown Fields Conservation Area. The proposed development is therefore contrary to policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), policies LP1, LP3 and LP5 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023) and the Housing SPD (2016). ",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development, by reason of design and layout, would afford future occupiers with a poor standard of accommodation due to the restricted outlook to Flat 4 and the lack of satisfactory private amenity space provision.The proposed development is therefore contrary to Policy LP27 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023).\r\n",
    "Reason : 4 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal.\r\n\r\n"
  ],
